 it suffices to show an inapproximability bound of the same type for just one parameter in each of the bottom three equivalence classes\r\nFor every $\\rho\\in \\{\\gamawtwo, \\gamasettwo, \\gamatsettwo, \\gamaR, \\rgamawtwo, \\rgamasettwo, \\rgamatsettwo\\}$ and every $\\epsilon >0$, there is no polynomial time algorithm approximating $\\rho$ for $n$-vertex split graphs without isolated vertices within a factor of \\hbox{$(1/2-\\epsilon)\\ln n$}, {unless ${\\sf P} = {\\sf NP}$.}\r\n$\\gama(G)\\le \\gamawtwo(G)\\le \\rgamawtwo(G)\\le\\gamaR(G)\\le \\rgamasettwo(G) = 2\\gama(G)$ and\r\nFor every $\\rho\\in \\{\\gamasettwo, \\gamatsettwo, \\rgamawtwo, \\gamaR, \\rgamasettwo, \\rgamatsettwo\\}$, there is a $2(\\ln(\\Delta(G)+2)+1)$-approximation algorithm for $\\rho$.\r\n\n"}
