{"step_index":105,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:39:44Z","thinking":"**Considering Dominating Vertices**\n\nFor each vertex $v$ in the set $V_2$, if $v$ has a neighbor also in $V_2$, then $V_2$ already dominates $v$. If $v$ lacks a neighbor in $V_2$, the graph's lack of isolated vertices guarantees $v$ has at least one neighbor, which can be added to the dominating set. Since each $v$ in $V_2$ has a function value of 2, adding the vertex and its neighbor is affordable, and these two vertices dominate $v$.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nimport itertools\n\n# Check if for EVERY Roman dominating function f on ANY graph G with no isolates,\n# gamma_t(G) <= weight(f).\n# Since gamma_R(G) = min weight(f), if gamma_t(G) <= gamma_R(G),\n# then since gamma_R(G) <= weight(f), gamma_t(G) <= weight(f) is AUTOMATICALLY true!\n# But the question is: is there an explicit S(f) with |S(f)| <= weight(f)?\n# Or does the proof use properties of MINIMUM weight f?\n\n# Let's test if there is an explicit mapping S(f)\nfor n in range(2, 8):\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n        if G.number_of_nodes() != n or any(G.degree(v) == 0 for v in G.nodes()):\n            continue\n        nodes = list(G.nodes())\n        # compute all total dominating sets\n        tds_list = []\n        for r in range(1, n+1):\n            for s in itertools.combinations(nodes, r):\n                if all(any(u in s for u in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\n                    tds_list.append(set(s))\n        min_tds = min(len(s) for s in tds_list)\n        \n        for f_tup in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n            f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tup))\n            if all(f[v] > 0 or any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\n                w = sum(f_tup)\n                if min_tds > w:\n                    print(f'FAILURE: min_tds = {min_tds} > weight = {w}')\n                    break\n\nprint('Checked all graphs up to n=7: gamma_t(G) <= weight(f) holds for EVERY Roman dominating function f!')\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing gamma_t <= weight(f) for all RDFs on all small graphs","toolSummary":"Test all RDFs small graphs"}}]}
